Add -autowindowresize / -noautowindowresize support.

Moonlight Embedded normally keeps the playback window fixed and scales video
inside it. That is the safe stock behavior, and remains the default. Korri's
Gamescope path needs the opposite policy: when the stream resolution changes,
the Moonlight surface should resize to the new video size so Gamescope owns the
upscale/filter step.

Add a single-dash Moonlight-style flag pair:

  -autowindowresize
  -noautowindowresize

The flag is surfaced to the v4l2m2m presenter through an internal environment
value before streaming starts. This keeps the runtime reset path local to the
video backend while preserving stock fixed-window behavior by default.

